      "description": "Any member, on a register with an open shift. A product line sold at another price than the store's catalog price needs an owner or a manager; the catalog price is kept with it. So do discounts over 10% (Settings → Users and roles): a line's own discount over 10% of the line, its share of a sale discount (`sale_discount_minor`) over 10% of it, or all the discounts over 10% of the items (gift cards are not counted); someone switched in with their PIN gives them as themselves. Totals and tax are worked out here from the lines; the payments must add up to what is due (the total less deposits already taken on the repairs it pays). Products leave stock (never below what open repairs hold), repairs are collected, store credit is used, and the sale gets the register's next receipt number. A card payment with `card_payment_id` must be approved, in this store, for the same amount, and not on another sale. A line with `gift_card` sells a gift card (no tax) and loads it; a `gift` payment takes from the card's balance, never below zero. Retry with the same Idempotency-Key after a lost answer: the sale is never recorded twice.",
